ute and the outside may open. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:18] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: If another defender steps across, a Spanish player can attack the space left behind. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:19] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: A useful football triangle does not need equal sides or 60-degree angles. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:20] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: Its best shape changes with defendersâ€™ positions, body orientation, ball speed and the space available. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:what-cabo-verde-s-world-cup-debut-means-for-african-football:1] What Cabo Verdeâ€™s World Cup debut means for African football: Cabo Verde lost to Argentina and exited the 2026 FIFA World Cup. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/what-cabo-verdes-world-cup-debut-means-for-african-football)\n  - [claim:what-cabo-verde-s-world-cup-debut-means-for-african-football:2] What Cabo Verdeâ€™s World Cup debut means for African football: As a former football player, lifelong lover of the beautiful game, and Cabo Verdean-American, watching Cabo Verde compete on the world stage for the first time felt bigger than sports. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/what-cabo-verdes-world-cup-debut-means-for-african-football)\n  - [claim:what-cabo-verde-s-world-cup-debut-means-for-african-football:3] What Cabo Verdeâ€™s World Cup debut means for African football: What this team represented went far beyond the final score. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/what-cabo-verdes-world-cup-debut-means-for-